        "html": "Speaking of Bryan, he was splendid. How on Earth he survived so long, it’s impossible to say, but it was very fun to watch. He encapsulates the stress of trying desperately to manage the fucked-up and grim situations you get thrown into in RE. Bryan is constantly panicked, resigned, and completely terrified. Truly, we’ve all been there, mate. His failure to properly wield a gun, manage his resources, or keep his fucking shit together is just pure fun. He also brings heart to the whole affair, with his tragic personal crisis and quite frankly abysmal luck. You really feel for him, even if you don’t get much chance to dwell on his emotional wellbeing. Also, he’s really quite cool in his own pathetic sorta way. A true everyman."
