        "html": "There is also that uniquely frightening experience that comes with getting lost. At the moment I’m at the coast, and every once in a while a Haar comes in, and I can’t see for shit. I could be 20m from shelter and miss it blindly in the fog. The same is true of blizzards, only that blizzards bring that awful cold. Having read <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/To_Build_a_Fire\">To Build A Fire</a> (and watched the TV adaptation of Dan Simmon’s <em>The Terror</em>), I have a healthy respect for the danger ice, snow and wind-chill brings. There is also the terrible darkness of night time out in nature. You might find the occasional gas lamp or wood-torch if you’re lucky. Early on in the game, though, you’ve got basically nothing. Perhaps a flare, which rapidly burns down to nothing. It is an awful feeling to be lost in the dark."
